report: "---\nauthor: \"builder\"\ncreated: \"2026-11-23\"\nupdated: \"2026-11-23\"\n---\n\n# Report: marshal-bytearray-rank-shim-fix\n\nDone. Branch `fix-marshal-bytearray-rank-shim` in the endojs/endo checkout,\nbased on master 679d9afaa. The job branch\n`job/marshal-bytearray-rank-shim-fix/2` points at the same head, 0e1b5945a.\nThere are two commits:\n\n- ada82e71b `fix(marshal): rank byteArrays by their bytes under the immutable-arraybuffer shim`.\n  Contains the fix, the marshal test and the changeset.\n- 0e1b5945a `test(patterns): compare and match equal-length byteArrays`\n\nThe commits are authored as `garden <garden@garden.invalid>` and carry a\n`Co-Authored-By` trailer. The steward re-attributes them when pushing.\n\n## Proposed pull request (draft, base master)\n\n**Title:** `fix(marshal): rank byteArrays by their bytes under the immutable-arraybuffer shim`\n\n**Body:**\n\n> ## What\n>\n> `compareRank` (in `packages/marshal/src/rankOrder.js`, case `'byteArray'`) now\n> always reads bytes through the buffer's own `slice(0)`. Before, it called\n> `new Uint8Array(buffer)` whenever `Object.getPrototypeOf(buffer) === ArrayBuffer.prototype`.\n>\n> ## Why\n>\n> Under `@endo/immutable-arraybuffer`, an emulated immutable buffer inherits\n> directly from `ArrayBuffer.prototype`, so it passes that check. But a\n> `Uint8Array` built on it views none of its bytes (length 0). Because of that,\n> any two byteArrays of the same length compared as 0, which breaks the\n> documented shortlex order. `compareKeys`, `keyEQ` and pattern matching in\n> `@endo/patterns` compare byteArrays through `compareRank`. So under the shim,\n> distinct byteArrays of the same length were also equal keys and matched each\n> other as patterns.\n>\n> The fix always copies. `@endo/bytes` has no compare function, and marshal\n> does not depend on it. The shim's brand is a private WeakMap, so marshal\n> cannot cheaply tell a native buffer from an emulated one. Checking\n> `immutable` would not help either, because native immutable buffers are\n> immutable too. The extra copy on the native path costs two `slice(0)` calls\n> per comparison of equal-length byteArrays, and the code stays obviously correct.\n>\n> ## Tests\n>\n> - `packages/marshal/test/rankOrder.test.js`: *compareRank orders equal-length\n>   byteArrays byte by byte*. Covers lengths 0, 1 and 3; a first difference at\n>   the start, middle and end; ties on equal bytes; both argument orders and\n>   `compareAntiRank`; shorter-first across lengths; and a `sortByRank`\n>   round-trip. The test logs which path is in use.\n> - `packages/patterns/test/byteArray-key-order.test.js`: `compareKeys`,\n>   `keyEQ` and `matches` (bare and nested in a copyArray) on equal-length\n>   byteArrays.\n>\n> Before the fix, both new tests fail. After it, they pass under all of\n> marshal's and patterns' ava configs (lockdown, unsafe, endo).\n>\n> On Node 22, `ArrayBuffer.prototype.sliceToImmutable` is not native, and\n> `ses`'s lockdown always installs the shim. So these tests exercise the\n> emulated path, which is the one with the bug. The native path cannot be\n> exercised on Node 22. The new test is written so it holds on either path.\n\n## What I ran\n\nAll of these ran in the checkout on Node v22.22.1, after\n`corepack yarn install`:\n\n- Reproduction, before the fix: under the shim, `getPrototypeOf(iab) === ArrayBuffer.prototype`\n  is `true`, `new Uint8Array(iab).length` is `0`, and\n  `compareRank([1], [2])` returns `0`.\n- New marshal test without the fix: failed (`0 < 1`, expected -1, got 0).\n  New patterns tests with only `rankOrder.js` reverted: both failed.\n- `ses-ava` in `packages/marshal`: 79 passed, 1 skipped (the\n  pre-existing `range queries` skip), in every config.\n- `ses-ava` in `packages/patterns`: 672 passed in every config.\n- `ses-ava` in `packages/pass-style` (not changed; run as a neighbor): all passed.\n- `tsc` and `eslint .` in marshal and patterns: exit 0, no errors. There are\n  4 warnings (`jsdoc/escape-inline-tags`), all in files I did not touch.\n- `prettier --check` on every changed file: clean.\n- `garden prose diff master`: no findings.\n\nSetup caveat: `yarn install` created no `node_modules/.bin`, so I called\n`ses-ava`, `ava`, `tsc` and `eslint` through small wrappers that run each\npackage's own `node_modules` copy. These are the same tools that\n`yarn test` and `yarn lint` run, just not invoked through yarn. I did not run\nCI (`act`).\n\n## Other places checked\n\n| Place | Reads bytes? | Verdict |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `marshal/src/rankOrder.js` `byteArray` | yes | the bug, fixed |\n| `marshal/src/encodePassable.js` `encodeByteArray` | no: throws \"not yet implemented\" | not affected |\n| `marshal/src/encodeToCapData.js`, `encodeToSmallcaps.js` | no: byteArray marshal throws \"not yet implemented\" | not affected |\n| `pass-style/src/byteArray.js` (brand check) | no: prototype, `immutable` getter, own keys | not affected |\n| `pass-style/src/deeplyFulfilled.js`, `typeGuards.js` | no: return or check style | not affected |\n| `patterns/src/keys/compareKeys.js` (`compareKeys`, `keyEQ`) | via `compareRank` | same bug, fixed by the marshal change, test added |\n| `patterns/src/patterns/patternMatchers.js` key matching, `M.byteArray` | key matching via `keyEQ`; the limit check uses only `byteLength` (the shim's accessor) | the first is fixed through `compareRank`, test added; the second is not affected |\n\nA grep for `new Uint8Array(` in the `src/` of marshal, pass-style and\npatterns finds only the two fixed lines.\n\nChangesets: `.changeset/bytearray-rank-shim.md`, `@endo/marshal: patch`.\n`@endo/patterns` gets no changeset, because only a test changed there; the\nmarshal changeset says the patterns behavior changes too.\n\n## Also\n\n- `roles/PLOT.md`: added a short note on the endo setup quirks in a slot.\n  These are: git's `safe.directory`; `COREPACK_HOME` outside the slot, because\n  the slot's `package.json` makes yarn load as ESM and crash; no\n  `node_modules/.bin`; and the commit identity.\n"
